# Local run & tests

## App (Next.js)

```bash
cd web
npm install   # first time / after lockfile changes
npm run dev   # http://localhost:3000
```

Room store defaults to `web/.data/rooms.json` when unset (see root `README.md`).

## Unit tests

```bash
cd web
npm run test:unit
```

## Gauge E2E (Playwright)

Requires the app on the target URL (default `http://localhost:3000` from `e2e/src/test/resources/config.toml`; override with `TARGET_URL`).

```bash
# terminal A — keep running
cd web && npm run dev

# terminal B
cd e2e
mise install
mise exec -- mvn test-compile
mise exec -- mvn gauge:execute
# one spec:
mise exec -- mvn -DspecsDir=specs/<name>.spec gauge:execute
```

Use `mise exec --` so Gauge/Java match `e2e/mise.toml`. Do not invent alternate runners.
